export const debate = {"id":"craig-clifton-kalam-cosmological-argument-2021","number":"126","assessmentModel":"5.6 Sol","assessmentRubric":"Slugfester Reassessment Rubric v2","title":"William Lane Craig vs Scott Clifton: The Kalam Cosmological Argument","label":"Kalam cosmological argument","date":"2026-08-18","duration":"1 hr 00 min","youtubeUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TmYCwjU_5Wc","motion":"Does the Kalam causal premise justify a transcendent cause of the universe, or is ordinary causation too bound to space, time, and material conditions to support that inference?","sourceNote":"Based on the complete debate transcript. Summaries are condensed for clarity, and quotations are kept brief and faithful to the source.","scoringNote":"Scores are AI-generated estimates of argumentative performance and are intended as transparent, revisable judgments rather than final verdicts.","summary":"Craig defends metaphysical causation beyond spacetime, while Clifton argues ordinary causal evidence supports narrower principles and leaves transcendent creation insufficiently warranted.","quotes":{"pro":{"text":"The argument leads, I think, to the existence of a","context":"Craig introduces the transcendent personal cause he believes follows from conceptual analysis of the Kalam conclusion."},"con":{"text":"the scope of the causal principle is physical and not metaphysical","context":"Clifton distinguishes observed intracosmic causation from the proposed application to spacetime considered as a totality."}},"sides":{"pro":{"name":"Kalam defense","speaker":"William Lane Craig","color":"teal"},"con":{"name":"Causal-scope critique","speaker":"Scott Clifton","color":"coral"}},"score":{"pro":82,"con":88},"sections":[{"sectionId":"causal-principle-scope","title":"Physical or Metaphysical Scope of the Causal Principle","timebox":"2:29–37:22","score":{"pro":83,"con":89},"exchanges":[{"pro":{"ledgerMoveId":"pro-kalam-causal-inference-and-transcendent-cause","time":"2:29","role":"Load-bearing constructive","words":"If the universe began and everything beginning has a cause, conceptual analysis indicates a beginningless, timeless, spaceless, immaterial, powerful, personal creator.","score":83,"critique":"Strongest feature: The opening presents a readily recoverable conditional inference, connects it directly to the motion, and identifies the proposed transcendent attributes with unusually economical argumentative organization. Principal limitation: Conceptual analysis is invoked more quickly than it is demonstrated, leaving the derivations of timelessness, immateriality, extraordinary power, and especially personality substantially compressed. Live burden: The defense must independently justify each attribute and show why a cause of spacetime should be personal rather than an impersonal metaphysical condition or foundational structure. Locked score: The strong/competent band reflects excellent relevance and clear inferential architecture, moderated by implicit qualifications, limited evidential development, and an ambitious conclusion whose several attribute-bridges remain incompletely articulated.","tags":[]},"con":{"ledgerMoveId":"con-physical-not-metaphysical-scope","time":"9:49","role":"Major direct reply","words":"Observed causation occurs within spacetime, so its evidential reach is physical rather than metaphysical and does not automatically encompass spacetime as a totality.","score":92,"critique":"Strongest feature: The reply isolates the debate's decisive scope transition, distinguishes physical evidence from metaphysical universality, and frames its conclusion as warranted withholding rather than categorical cosmic acausality. Principal limitation: Restricting evidential reach does not itself establish that the underlying causal principle lacks metaphysical status, because conceptual or modal support could supplement the acknowledged observational limitation. Live burden: The critique must answer the independent being-from-nonbeing rationale and explain whether cosmic uniqueness defeats inference altogether or merely reduces confidence in extrapolation beyond familiar conditions. Locked score: The very strong band reflects direct motion contact, unusually precise domain control, and proportionate calibration, tempered only by the surviving possibility of a nonempirical justification for broader causal scope.","tags":[]}},{"pro":{"ledgerMoveId":"pro-metaphysical-scope-being-from-nonbeing","time":"36:03","role":"Load-bearing constructive","words":"The causal principle is metaphysical, not merely scientific: being cannot arise from nonbeing, so whatever genuinely comes into existence requires a cause.","score":82,"critique":"Strongest feature: The reply directly supplies the nonempirical route left open by the physical-scope objection, stating a stable metaphysical principle and connecting it clearly to the causal conclusion. Principal limitation: Rooted intuition and traditional formulation do not by themselves establish necessity, while describing an unexplained initial boundary as emergence from nothing may already favor the disputed causal interpretation. Live burden: The defense must distinguish explanatory absence from ontological production by nothing and provide a noncircular reason that every genuine beginning requires an efficient cause. Locked score: The strong/competent band reflects decisive relevance, precise statement, and a substantial answer to empirical restriction, reduced because the necessity claim remains largely asserted and risks incorporating its conclusion into the description of beginning.","tags":[{"label":"Begging the question","type":"fallacy","url":"https://logfall.com/fallacies/begging-the-question/","context":"Characterizing an unexplained initial boundary as being produced from nonbeing risks presupposing the causal reading that the argument must establish."}]},"con":{"ledgerMoveId":"con-ordinary-causal-features-absent","time":"13:55","role":"Major direct reply","words":"Cosmic creation lacks several features of observed causation: occurrence within spacetime, efficient-material interaction, and an intelligible relation in which something is affected.","score":86,"critique":"Strongest feature: The reply accumulates several concrete disanalogies between ordinary causal episodes and cosmic creation, reinforcing the scope objection through identifiable experiential features rather than unsupported incredulity. Principal limitation: The underdefined affect-effect terminology risks conflating alteration of preexisting material with production of an effect, while common empirical accompaniment is not automatically metaphysical necessity. Live burden: The critique must explain why spacetime location, material interaction, or a previously affected entity constitutes causation rather than merely characterizing the familiar instances from which humans learn causation. Locked score: The very strong band reflects precise comparative relevance, explicit intuitive calibration, and substantial empirical grounding, moderated by the remaining need for a principled necessity-bridge from observed features to every possible causal relation.","tags":[]}}]},{"sectionId":"material-cause-and-agent-causation","title":"Material Accompaniment and Immaterial Agent Causation","timebox":"6:35–30:18","score":{"pro":80,"con":85},"exchanges":[{"pro":{"ledgerMoveId":"pro-agent-causation-without-material-cause","time":"15:42","role":"Major direct reply","words":"An intellectual agent's production of thoughts suggests that material accompaniment is common, not essential, because thoughts are not constituted from material stuff.","score":82,"critique":"Strongest feature: The mental-event example directly challenges material accompaniment as a necessary condition of efficient causation and supplies an intelligible countermodel involving familiar personal agency. Principal limitation: Nonconstitution by matter does not demonstrate independence from material brains, and producing mental events may not relevantly model an immaterial agent producing concrete substances without antecedent conditions. Live burden: The defense must establish genuinely nonmaterial causal production and explain why its structure transfers from thought generation to creation of a universe rather than merely illustrating conceptual dependence. Locked score: The strong/competent band reflects direct responsiveness, clear counterexample structure, and appropriately possibility-level force, reduced by a disputed philosophy-of-mind premise and an incompletely defended transition from mental events to concrete cosmic reality.","tags":[]},"con":{"ledgerMoveId":"con-material-cause-parity","time":"6:35","role":"Major direct reply","words":"Induction supporting efficient causes equally supports material accompaniment, so empirical evidence alone cannot justify retaining the efficient-cause principle while rejecting its material counterpart.","score":88,"critique":"Strongest feature: The parity construction precisely targets the inductive warrant for the causal premise, formulates a parallel material principle, and carefully avoids claiming that material causation is metaphysically necessary. Principal limitation: The empirical sample is treated as representative without examining counterexamples, competing causal classifications, or whether observed material accompaniment is evidentially separable from ordinary efficient production. Live burden: The critique must show that the parity survives a defense of the Kalam premise as metaphysical intuition rather than empirical generalization, since induction alone is its expressly limited target. Locked score: The very strong band reflects exceptional responsiveness, stable scope, and disciplined calibration, while recognizing that ordinary-case parity does not independently defeat a separately warranted metaphysical principle.","tags":[]}},{"pro":{"ledgerMoveId":"pro-efficient-explanation-better-than-double-absence","time":"19:55","role":"Supporting constructive","words":"A transcendent personal agent could cause concrete reality without prior matter, whereas an uncaused beginning would possess neither an efficient cause nor a material cause.","score":78,"critique":"Strongest feature: The contrast places explanatory alternatives side by side and emphasizes that an immaterial efficient cause could, if independently coherent, avoid leaving the universe wholly causally unexplained. Principal limitation: Describing double absence as absurd overstates the comparison, because brute initial existence remains logically coherent and the proposed thought-to-concrete-production mechanism receives little supporting analysis. Live burden: The defense must provide positive grounds for personal agency beyond the dissatisfaction generated by absent causes and show how intention produces concrete reality without presupposing the disputed capacity. Locked score: The strong/competent band reflects relevant explanatory comparison and clear engagement with material parity, constrained by implicit causal mechanics, overstated rhetoric, and insufficient evidence that personal production is preferable to brute existence.","tags":[]},"con":{"ledgerMoveId":"con-effect-without-affected-thing","time":"29:10","role":"Major direct reply","words":"Creation without efficient-material interaction posits an effect while nothing antecedently is affected, making transcendent causation less intelligible than physically restricted causation.","score":80,"critique":"Strongest feature: The reply identifies a specific intelligibility problem for creation without matter by asking what causal production means when no preexisting entity undergoes alteration or receives influence. Principal limitation: The terminology equivocally approaches two meanings of affected: something previously changed and something newly produced as an effect, so the objection may embed its preferred causal model. Live burden: The critique must demonstrate that alteration of an antecedent subject is constitutive of causation rather than a pervasive feature of transformation cases observed within the physical universe. Locked score: The strong/competent band reflects direct engagement, recoverable conceptual pressure, and measured presentation, tempered by unstable terminology and the absence of a decisive argument excluding productive causation that originates rather than modifies its object.","tags":[{"label":"Equivocation","type":"fallacy","url":"https://logfall.com/fallacies/equivocation/","context":"The objection materially shifts between an antecedent thing being altered and a newly produced thing counting as the causal effect."}]}}]},{"sectionId":"temporal-beginning-and-cosmic-boundary","title":"Temporal Beginning and the Universe's Boundary","timebox":"11:29–52:32","score":{"pro":86,"con":90},"exchanges":[{"pro":{"ledgerMoveId":"pro-boundary-compatible-definition-of-beginning","time":"11:29","role":"Major direct reply","words":"Something begins at a time when no earlier time contains it; this permits time and the universe to begin without requiring a preceding empty interval.","score":83,"critique":"Strongest feature: The proposed definition clearly permits a first temporal boundary without presupposing earlier time, thereby answering the apparent contradiction in saying that time itself genuinely begins. Principal limitation: This semantic and conceptual clarification does not answer the stronger evidential objection that causal experience concerns processes occurring within spacetime rather than the origin of spacetime. Live burden: The defense must establish why this definition is preferable to rival boundary descriptions and then provide an independent bridge from coherent beginning to metaphysically required causation. Locked score: The strong/competent band reflects high coherence, explicit qualification, and indispensable support for the boundary-beginning route, offset by partial responsiveness to the opponent's central physical-scope challenge and limited uniqueness warrant.","tags":[]},"con":{"ledgerMoveId":"con-temporally-exhaustive-universe","time":"30:59","role":"Major direct reply","words":"A universe existing at every temporal point is not relevantly like an object popping into existence within time, so ordinary appearance intuitions do not transfer.","score":89,"critique":"Strongest feature: The reply sharply distinguishes temporal exhaustiveness from intratemporal appearance and thereby exposes misleading imagery in comparisons between a first universe and ordinary objects suddenly materializing. Principal limitation: Saying that beginning language cannot apply is stronger than showing that its familiar imagery misleads, because rival temporal theories can describe objective becoming at the first moment. Live burden: The critique must explain why existence at every temporal point precludes genuine becoming rather than merely precluding an earlier empty interval, especially under a tensed conception of time. Locked score: The very strong band reflects precise scope, excellent responsiveness, and a powerful structural distinction, while leaving unresolved the theory-dependent metaphysics of whether a first temporal boundary constitutes coming into being.","tags":[]}},{"pro":{"ledgerMoveId":"pro-tensed-becoming-from-being-principle","time":"32:30","role":"Major direct reply","words":"On a tensed theory, the universe genuinely comes into being rather than having a static front edge, and being cannot arise uncaused from nonbeing.","score":88,"critique":"Strongest feature: The response directly addresses the static-front-edge interpretation by making its temporal theory explicit and connecting objective becoming to the metaphysical principle that being cannot originate from nonbeing. Principal limitation: The success is conditional upon a tensed theory that the excerpt does not establish, while the causal interpretation of being-from-nonbeing remains philosophically contestable rather than analytically compulsory. Live burden: The defense must argue for objective temporal becoming and demonstrate that a first moment without an antecedent cause is properly characterized as being arising from nonbeing. Locked score: The very strong band reflects excellent directness, stable theoretical qualification, and coherent metaphysical integration, moderated by dependence on an undefended temporal framework and a substantive causal principle still requiring independent support.","tags":[]},"con":{"ledgerMoveId":"con-no-prior-empty-interval","time":"52:05","role":"Major direct reply","words":"A universe present at every temporal point differs from one appearing after empty time; only the latter resembles a sudden, uncaused intrusion.","score":91,"critique":"Strongest feature: The reply supplies an exceptionally clear temporal discriminator, contrasting an antecedent empty interval followed by appearance with a universe that exists throughout the entire temporal domain. Principal limitation: The distinction establishes different temporal structures but does not independently refute the tensed-theory claim that a first moment can involve objective becoming without any earlier interval. Live burden: The critique must show why temporal exhaustiveness bears on causal dependence and whether it supports acausality rather than merely dissolving an inaccurate picture of delayed cosmic arrival. Locked score: The very strong band reflects outstanding directness, stable scope, strong evidential illustration, and decisive pressure on the popping analogy, tempered only by the surviving metaphysical question of theory-relative becoming at the boundary.","tags":[]}}]},{"sectionId":"restricted-causal-alternatives","title":"Restricted Causal Principles and Ordinary Regularity","timebox":"39:21–58:23","score":{"pro":80,"con":89},"exchanges":[{"pro":{"ledgerMoveId":"pro-substance-event-causation-distinction","time":"49:52","role":"Major direct reply","words":"The Kalam premise concerns substances beginning to exist and does not commit its defender to the distinct proposition that every event has a cause.","score":89,"critique":"Strongest feature: The reply precisely limits the Kalam commitment to substances and thereby blocks an event-based parity objection without denying that separate reasons might support or undermine universal event causation. Principal limitation: The distinction answers only the event formulation and does not resolve restricted principles distinguishing initial from non-initial substances or spacetime-internal from cosmic beginnings. Live burden: The defense must show that substance beginnings share a relevant causal requirement across the contested boundary while addressing class restrictions that operate entirely within the category of substances. Locked score: The very strong band reflects exceptional precision, direct logical support, explicit qualification, and charitable engagement, moderated only because its relevance is subsidiary and its successful distinction leaves the opponent's strongest substance-based alternatives untouched.","tags":[]},"con":{"ledgerMoveId":"con-restricted-causal-principles","time":"39:21","role":"Load-bearing constructive","words":"Causal requirements limited to non-initial things or beginnings within spacetime preserve ordinary regularity without committing to an unrestricted metaphysical causal principle.","score":89,"critique":"Strongest feature: The move offers explicit alternatives rather than merely rejecting universality, showing how ordinary stability can be preserved by principles limited to non-initial entities or spacetime-internal beginnings. Principal limitation: Demonstrating that restricted formulations are logically available does not establish their truth, modal grounding, explanatory superiority, or immunity from concerns about an artificially tailored cosmic exception. Live burden: The critique must justify the selected restriction independently and explain why initiality or spacetime location is causally relevant rather than simply describing the disputed case. Locked score: The very strong band reflects concrete constructive alternatives, disciplined possibility-level calibration, and direct support for the restricted-principles route, tempered by the absence of an independent metaphysical account establishing which restriction accurately governs reality.","tags":[]}},{"pro":{"ledgerMoveId":"pro-no-prior-restrictor-of-uncaused-beginnings","time":"57:29","role":"Major direct reply","words":"If things can begin uncaused from nothing, nothing explanatorily prior exists to restrict which kinds may do so, undermining selective causal alternatives.","score":74,"critique":"Strongest feature: The reply accepts the impossibility burden directly and offers a definite rationale, contending that wholly uncaused beginnings lack any explanatorily prior reality capable of imposing selective restrictions. Principal limitation: The inference assumes that every restriction requires a prior entity, overlooking necessary natures, constitutive truths, modal structures, or noncausal facts that need not temporally precede anything. Live burden: The defense must define explanatory priority and show why non-temporal or structural grounds cannot differentiate possible beginnings before claiming that a selective explanation is impossible. Locked score: The mixed band reflects strong responsiveness and central relevance alongside materially overstated necessity, unstable explanatory terminology, insufficient engagement with decisive alternatives, and comparatively weak coherence and charitable representation.","tags":[]},"con":null}]},{"sectionId":"selective-uncaused-existence","title":"Selective Uncaused Existence and the Arbitrary-Objects Challenge","timebox":"48:07–55:33","score":{"pro":80,"con":87},"exchanges":[{"pro":{"ledgerMoveId":"pro-arbitrary-objects-challenge","time":"48:07","role":"Diagnostic challenge","words":"If the universe may begin uncaused, no supplied restriction explains why bicycles, root beer, or other arbitrary objects cannot likewise begin without causes.","score":80,"critique":"Strongest feature: The vivid examples convert an abstract exception into a focused explanatory demand, pressing the opponent to identify a principled difference between the universe and arbitrary intracosmic substances. Principal limitation: The suggestion that one exception leaves no possible restriction substantially outruns the argument, because initiality, temporal location, modal nature, or structural classification could differentiate the cases. Live burden: The challenge must evaluate those proposed distinctions and show their irrelevance rather than treating permission for one exceptional class as permission for every conceivable object. Locked score: The strong/competent band reflects direct pressure on selective acausality, memorable clarity, and substantial route relevance, reduced by overstatement, incomplete engagement with available class restrictions, and a conditional inference requiring further defense.","tags":[]},"con":{"ledgerMoveId":"con-principled-exception-parity","time":"50:44","role":"Major direct reply","words":"One special class of uncaused occurrences need not license unrelated uncaused objects, just as possible uncaused mental events would not predict arbitrary physical events.","score":87,"critique":"Strongest feature: The reply defeats the claimed entailment from one exceptional class to universal permissibility and effectively uses the opponent's willingness to distinguish mental events as a structural parity example. Principal limitation: Showing that class-specific exceptions can be coherent does not identify the actual principle distinguishing an uncaused universe from arbitrary substances or demonstrate that the comparison is cosmically relevant. Live burden: The critique must supply and defend a non-ad-hoc classifier, such as initiality or temporal exhaustiveness, rather than resting on the formal possibility of principled exceptions. Locked score: The very strong band reflects excellent responsiveness, calibrated non-entailment, and a pertinent counterexample, while acknowledging that the deeper explanatory demand for a warranted universe-specific distinction remains unresolved.","tags":[]}},{"pro":null,"con":{"ledgerMoveId":"con-inexplicability-burden","time":"55:07","role":"Diagnostic challenge","words":"Calling selective uncaused existence inexplicable asserts that no explanation is possible, placing an especially demanding modal burden on the claimant.","score":86,"critique":"Strongest feature: The response precisely separates requesting an explanation from asserting that explanation is impossible, correctly identifying the substantially heavier modal burden carried by the latter formulation. Principal limitation: The burden shift applies only to the strongest reading of inexplicability and does not answer the weaker, still relevant complaint that no principled selective explanation has actually been supplied. Live burden: The critique must preserve this semantic distinction while confronting the ordinary explanatory demand rather than allowing a modal clarification to substitute for a positive account of cosmic exceptionality. Locked score: The very strong band reflects conceptual precision, proportionate calibration, and direct diagnostic value, moderated by subsidiary route importance and incomplete resolution of the underlying request for an explanation.","tags":[]}}]}],"overall":{"pro":{"score":82,"strengths":["Clearly framed the Kalam inference and connected the universe's beginning to the proposed transcendent explanation.","Supplied a coherent boundary-compatible definition of beginning without requiring an earlier empty time.","Directly answered material-cause parity with an agent-causation counterexample and separated substances from events.","Developed the metaphysical being-from-nonbeing rationale that an empirical-scope objection alone leaves open."],"blunders":[{"text":"The derivation from a cosmic cause to a personal creator remained compressed, leaving several attribute-bridges insufficiently defended.","links":[]},{"text":"The final no-prior-restrictor argument overlooked necessary, structural, and noncausal grounds that need not antecede the universe.","links":[]}]},"con":{"score":88,"strengths":["Precisely distinguished evidence about physical causation from a universal metaphysical causal principle.","Constructed a strong material-cause parity argument while limiting its conclusion to the reach of induction.","Sharply separated a temporally exhaustive universe from an object appearing after an earlier empty interval.","Offered concrete restricted causal principles and carefully diagnosed the modal burden created by claims of inexplicability."],"blunders":[{"text":"The affected-thing objection left its central causal terminology underdefined and did not establish that antecedent alteration is essential to causation.","links":[{"label":"Equivocation","url":"https://logfall.com/fallacies/equivocation/"}]},{"text":"The principled-exception reply established non-entailment but did not supply an independently warranted principle distinguishing the universe from arbitrary objects.","links":[]}]}},"logicalExtension":{"pro":{"finalArgument":{"thesis":"The AI steelman is that a genuine first temporal boundary is best explained by a nonphysical agent only if a modest causal principle and a separate agency inference are independently defended.","premises":["If a concrete reality genuinely begins, explanatory dependence is presumptively appropriate unless a relevant feature of that reality defeats the presumption.","A first temporal boundary can count as a beginning without an earlier empty interval, because earlier nonexistence need not occur at an earlier time.","Physical disanalogies weaken induction but do not settle whether explanation, dependence, and productive agency can apply beyond spacetime under a broader metaphysical account.","If the originating explanation is not a prior physical state or timelessly sufficient impersonal condition, purposive agency becomes one candidate explanation, though not a deduction from causation alone."],"conclusion":"Accordingly, the universe's genuine beginning supplies a defeasible case for a nonphysical explanation and, conditionally, for agency, without establishing every traditional divine attribute from the causal conclusion alone."},"newArguments":[{"title":"Contrastive origin and agency","text":"An impersonal timeless condition that is wholly sufficient for a universe seems unable, without an additional differentiating fact, to explain why a temporally finite reality obtains rather than an equally timeless effect. Agency offers a contrastive structure: an intention can explain the obtaining of one contingent outcome without requiring a prior material trigger. This does not prove a creator, but it gives personality an independent explanatory role instead of deriving it merely from the word cause."},{"title":"Defeasible explanatory presumption","text":"The causal premise can be reformulated as a defeasible explanatory norm: concrete beginnings call for explanation unless a relevant defeater is supplied. Cosmic uniqueness then blocks simple statistical induction without automatically defeating the norm, while the defender must openly compare candidate defeaters such as necessary initiality, brute facthood, or structural constraint. This formulation avoids claiming that observation mechanically proves metaphysical universality and makes the disagreement turn on identified defeaters rather than competing intuitions alone."}]},"con":{"finalArgument":{"thesis":"The AI steelman is that ordinary causal evidence underdetermines cosmic origins, so rational restraint favors a boundary-neutral explanation policy over a transcendent personal inference.","premises":["Every ordinary case informing causal judgment occurs within an existing physical order whose spacetime, laws, fields, or materials already constrain the interaction.","The beginning of the entire physical order lacks those background conditions, making it a domain shift for which ordinary causal frequency supplies limited direct guidance.","Existence at every temporal point differs from appearing after empty time, so ordinary intuitions about sudden intratemporal objects do not decide the boundary case.","Restricted principles can explain ordinary stability, but their restriction must be defended through domain structure rather than asserted merely to exempt the universe."],"conclusion":"Therefore, the available causal evidence supports withholding the transcendent personal inference while leaving open whether the cosmic boundary has a cause, a structural explanation, or brute status."},"newArguments":[{"title":"Boundary-model underdetermination","text":"Several importantly different models can fit the same temporal fact that the universe has a first moment: external efficient production, a necessary boundary condition, a brute initial state, or a noncausal structural explanation. The first-moment fact alone does not discriminate among them. A personal creator consequently requires evidence that favors agency over these alternatives, not merely the elimination of an earlier physical cause. This comparative requirement strengthens restraint without asserting that any rival model is already correct."},{"title":"Domain-sensitive causal induction","text":"Induction is most reliable when the target resembles the sampled domain in the properties relevant to the regularity. Cosmic origin differs from ordinary production in lacking an antecedent spacetime, shared laws, and established material context. Those differences do not prove that causation fails, but they reduce the evidential force of extrapolation. A domain-sensitive policy therefore permits robust causal expectations inside the universe while assigning substantially wider uncertainty to the boundary, without inventing arbitrary exceptions for bicycles or other later objects."}]}},"year":2021};
